From f9eaba498866b710dd1952af61c6d0898d185b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:20:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] C-80 defects 3+4: capacity counts
 cir.compile/gate.certify against their lane (inputs.cir.slug) and enforces
 the #30 mix on measured job-seconds with largest-remainder slot budgets

- swarm/capacity.slug_of reads inputs.slug / product_slug / cir.slug, used at the claim, in
  measured_lane_split and in release._lane_capacity's starved-lane boost
- function_budgets shares the pool by largest remainder (min one slot each); share_decision
  also holds a function that has run more than its target share of the last 24h job-seconds
  while an under-share function has runnable work and the pool is in use
- tests: three new handler-level tests through Worker.run_once; the gate.lanes test's
  UNMEASURED assertion is strengthened to a measured split (the uncounted certify runs were
  the bug)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
