Subject: [PATCH 2/7] C-80 defects 1, 2, 5, 16, 17(part): size depth read from
 the CIRs' own grading, thrash backoff increments only on a new unchanged
 observation, lab provenance filtered by version, _progress bounded in SQL

- cir/graded.size_run counts the certified releases in a design's size run (graded
  concept_key siblings or size-variant titles), MEASURED, or UNMEASURED for an unreadable CIR;
  commerce/lanes._sizes_of and teardown/lab customization read it (no phantom 'sizes' key)
- swarm/orchestrate._free_poll_backoff stores last_counted_job_id; a sweep with no new run
  keeps level, factor and the absolute deadline; a new unchanged run doubles and extends
- tests/test_cert_thrash.py: the assertion that enshrined the doubling (factor 4 after a sweep
  with nothing new) now asserts factor 2 / deadline kept, then factor 4 on a new run
- teardown/lab: ArtefactProvenance read for slug@version only (Codex P05)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
